ated to the atrial fibrillation detection pathway."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec3-risk-management-system", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Highlights the requirement for continuous risk management and updating based on post-market surveillance."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2019A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Telemetry review log showing a pattern of irregularities adjacent to the atrial fibrillation detection pathway."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2012A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Telemetry review log showing ventricular tachycardia-adjacent irregularity, release v12 - further evidence of potential signal processing issues."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "While the immediate clinical exposure was prevented by the CI/CD gate, the incident report highlights a recurring telemetry irregularity (ARTIFACT-INCIDENT-2026B) and a validation finding (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2011A). The automated gate successfully contained the issue, preventing patient harm. However, the recurrence of this irregularity, as indicated by the second confirmed ventricular fibrillation miss report, suggests an underlying problem with the atrial fibrillation detection pathway that requires further investigation. The risk management system (ID: mdr-annexI-sec3-risk-management-system) mandates continuous iterative updating based on post-market surveillance data. The telemetry logs (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2019A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2012A) demonstrate a pattern of irregularities adjacent to the atrial fibrillation detection pathway, indicating potential issues with signal processing or interpretation. Although no patient was directly exposed, the recurring nature of the issue and the validation finding necessitate a CAPA_INVESTIGATE to determine the root cause and prevent future occurrences. The regulatory context (ID: qmsr-820.35-records) emphasizes the importance of recording and investigating complaints related to device failures; this incident falls under that requirement.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "ab1211e260f778810888794df8243b165a43b663005d9d38776a5668b5cfca70", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0006", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0006_r3", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0006", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 2, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T15:25:48.024212Z", "total_steps": 5, "trace_id": "05f3d719-fd59-4634-87fd-5312f0864e39"}
